# The image's build context (EXIT-RUNBOOK.md). A file left out here is a file
# `docker build` never sees: the image installs its own node_modules from the
# lockfile and runs its own `next build`, so nothing built on the host leaks in.

# Installed and built inside the image.
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Never in an image: history, secrets, session files, scratch output.
.git
.env*
.vercel
.claude
.topdeck-raw
.optcg-images
scripts/.tmp
coverage

# The planning corpus. Tailwind's automatic source detection reads every
# text file in the context for class names, and these quote classes no
# component uses (LATER.md row 217), so the image's CSS is the clean one:
# smaller than the Vercel build's by exactly those dead rules.
**/*.md

# Read by the Docker CLI, not by the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
